#. manifest, tekst 14
#: app/templates/manifest.html:80
msgid "Long-term perspective"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 1
#: app/templates/manifest.html:94
msgid "Major powers pay too little attention to international law. The Global Union (GU) offers an alternative: a permanent cooperation between functioning democracies, as a complement to the EU and the UN. Together we want to use our market power for prosperity, social security, a liveable planet, security and the enforcement of international agreements."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 2
#: app/templates/manifest.html:95
msgid "Any country that scores well on democracy, the rule of law, human rights and anti-corruption can join. A solid foundation already exists. In October 2026, the EU and Canada formed an alliance for the future. Like-minded countries have been invited to join. Together, our economy is more than one third of the world's and larger than that of the US."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 3
#: app/templates/manifest.html:96
msgid "The GU is principled and pragmatic. Principled, because trade tariffs depend on how a country scores on honouring international agreements and shared values. Countries that meet all criteria pay no import duties. Countries that commit aggression are excluded. Pragmatic, because we start small, with limited tariffs. We want to be attractive and avoid unnecessary escalation. This gives us time to become strategically independent together."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 4
#: app/templates/manifest.html:97
msgid "Those who join benefit. That gives countries a reason to reform, as happened earlier with the EU. This is how the union grows: through attraction."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, tekst 16
#: app/templates/manifest.html:103
msgid "Core principles of the Global Union"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, tekst 17
#: app/templates/manifest.html:107
msgid "A values-driven trade system"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, tekst 18
#: app/templates/manifest.html:109
msgid "The GU operates with a single system of trade tariffs based on a scorecard per country, measured on:"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, lijstitem 5
#. manifest, tabelkop 63
#: app/templates/manifest.html:112 app/templates/manifest.html:278
msgid "Anti-corruption"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, lijstitem 6
#: app/templates/manifest.html:113
msgid "Freedom: rule of law, democracy, free press"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, lijstitem 7
#. manifest, tabelkop 60
#: app/templates/manifest.html:114 app/templates/manifest.html:273
msgid "Human rights"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, lijstitem 8
#: app/templates/manifest.html:115
msgid "Sustainability: climate accords, respect for nature"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, lijstitem 9
#: app/templates/manifest.html:116
msgid "Conduct within the international legal order: IP protection, no espionage, no dumping, contribution to the International Court of Justice"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 10
#: app/templates/manifest.html:120
#, python-format
msgid "Countries that fully comply pay %(rate)s import duties. Countries that partially comply pay based on their score, with yearly measurement and adjustment. Countries that commit aggression or murder their own people are fully excluded, and countries that continue to trade with them face higher tariffs."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, tekst 19
#: app/templates/manifest.html:125
msgid "Peaceful but firm foreign policy"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 11
#: app/templates/manifest.html:128
msgid "The GU invests in strategic independence for all members: raw materials, energy, defence and its own AI capabilities. The GU must urgently stand on its own two feet in these areas."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 12
#: app/templates/manifest.html:129
msgid "The GU does not pursue assertive military action, unless a broad majority of GU members judges intervention necessary because of crimes against a country's own population. Democratisation in autocratic countries happens through uprising from within the population itself. If regimes misbehave, we support the opposition."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, tekst 20
#: app/templates/manifest.html:134
msgid "Information freedom as a strategic instrument"
msgstr ""

#. manifest, tekst 21
#: app/templates/manifest.html:136
msgid "The GU extends its influence through high-quality independent journalism in all local languages - by analogy to the BBC, reinforced with GU resources - and by making protected technology available that frees people from state-controlled internet access."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 13
#: app/templates/manifest.html:143
msgid "The GU does not function as a single market with full free movement of people, to avoid unwanted migration flows toward wealthier areas. Uniform trade tariffs based on the scorecard do apply."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 14
#: app/templates/manifest.html:144
msgid "For high-value work, we issue temporary work visas to scarce talent from GU countries as well as from non-GU countries. The principle is circular: those who work abroad temporarily bring knowledge, experience and networks back to their home country."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 15
#: app/templates/manifest.html:145
msgid "The GU also invests in training programmes through which people in non-GU countries can develop to the level needed to make a valuable contribution. Once back home, they can continue to contribute to the GU economy remotely. This way prosperity grows on both sides."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 16
#: app/templates/manifest.html:153
msgid "Accession is tied to three existing, independent indices: the Democracy Index, the Corruption Perceptions Index, and the Human Rights Index. For each index, a 'sufficient' level and a 'minimum' level have been chosen. The minimum level is chosen so that the EU can join as a bloc."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 17
#: app/templates/manifest.html:154
msgid "Countries above the minimum level are invited to join."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 18
#: app/templates/manifest.html:155
msgid "Three countries receive separate treatment. The United States and Israel are not invited for now. These countries do numerically meet the standard, but it cannot be expected that, under their current administrations, they would want to commit to the rules of the Global Union. Taiwan also qualifies, but lacks UN-recognised status. For this we can work with a separate status, as is already the case at the WTO."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, alinea 19
#: app/templates/manifest.html:156
msgid "The indices carry a limited margin of error. Countries that fall just short of the threshold can still be assessed on request."
msgstr ""

#. manifest, tekst 24
#: app/templates/manifest.html:160
msgid "View the full list of all 183 countries and their scores"
